WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:03.600
The conclusion of "Black Adam"&nbsp;
leaves its characters in very&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.580
interesting places for future DCEU movies.&nbsp;
But what about Pierce Brosnan's Dr. Fate?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.920
The following contains spoilers for "Black Adam."

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:16.560
Besides Dwayne Johnson's soundstage-shaking frame&nbsp;
filling most of the scenes of "Black Adam," the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.120
hierarchy of power in the DC universe hasn't&nbsp;
so much as changed as it has spread out with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.980
the addition of the Justice Society of America.&nbsp;
Besides marking the first big-screen iteration of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:31.140
Black Adam, the film also marks the arrival of the&nbsp;
classic superteam. This iteration features Carter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:37.260
Hall, aka Hawkman, Cyclone, Atom Smasher, and&nbsp;
the stoic, Doctor Fate played by Pierce Brosnan.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.920
In "Black Adam," it's established early&nbsp;
on that both Carter and the good Doctor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:46.320
also known as Kent Nelson, go way back. The wise&nbsp;
old mystic is much older than he appears, living&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.230
a life riddled with harrowing visions of bleak&nbsp;
futures that he's thankfully managed to avoid.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:53.278
"My vision has shown me the future."

00:00:53.278 --> 00:00:58.020
However, the reawakening of an ancient force&nbsp;
paves the way for a fate that not everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:02.640
will be able to outrun, leading Nelson&nbsp;
to take drastic steps to avoid it. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.160
with the dust settled, what's&nbsp;
Doctor Fate's prognosis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:09.240
and what does it mean for the future of&nbsp;
the DCEU on the verge of making a comeback?

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:13.500
If you've got this far, you've no doubt checked&nbsp;
"Black Adam" off your watchlist and seen that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:17.820
Brosnan's charming master of magic sacrificed&nbsp;
himself to get Black Adam back in the fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.820 --> 00:01:21.720
It's a bit of a shame the former Bond's&nbsp;
involvement in the franchise was so brief&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:26.280
after being considered a highlight following the&nbsp;
film's release. All that's left now is an empty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:31.260
chair on Carter Hall's decked-out Cruiser and a&nbsp;
helmet without an owner. Well, for now, at least.

00:01:31.260 --> 00:01:34.680
In the comics, the Helmet of Fate&nbsp;
has had many owners over the years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.240
with Nelson being one of its most notable.&nbsp;
Even those not explicitly chosen to don the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:43.560
helm have tried on the headgear, including&nbsp;
dry-witted Hellblazer John Constantine and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.940
even Superman himself. On some occasions,&nbsp;
however, the helm has been a perfect fit for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.080
other heroes donning the mantle of Doctor&nbsp;
Fate. Nelson's own bloodline has stepped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:56.040
up to take over, and there have even been&nbsp;
total newcomers to the game of good, evil,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.040 --> 00:02:01.260
and hand-wavey magic spells. However, among those&nbsp;
contributing to Fate's legacy is a contender that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:06.240
given a little bit of tweaking here and there,&nbsp;
could be located not far from Adam's home turf.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:10.080
Currently, in the comics, the doctor on&nbsp;
duty isn't Kent Nelson but his nephew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:15.720
Khalid Nassour. Debuting in 2015, Khalid is an&nbsp;
Egyptian-American who has been linked to many of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:21.000
DC's superteams beyond just the Justice Society.&nbsp;
Currently, he's a member of Justice League Dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.220
a united force against the demonic and hellish&nbsp;
threats to humanity and led by none other than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.220 --> 00:02:30.540
John Constantine. Considering the character&nbsp;
is set to return to the big screen with Keanu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.540 --> 00:02:35.040
Reeves reprising the role, it feels almost like&nbsp;
fate that the next in line for that shiny gold&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:39.300
helmet is part of a team that Warner Bros. has&nbsp;
been wanting to bring to live-action for years.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:44.160
With Constantine coming back to exorcise some&nbsp;
demons and a helmet without a hero to don it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:48.960
"Black Adam" feels like a great stepping-off&nbsp;
point to establish another new area of the DC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:53.400
universe that is fighting to make a comeback.&nbsp;
Also, given Khalid's Egyptian heritage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.480
it'd be cool if his origin story could be&nbsp;
altered and he somehow winds up in Kahndaq&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:01.740
to meet Black Adam just like his uncle did.&nbsp;
Who knows? The hierarchy of power in the DC&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.520
universe might be changing after all, and&nbsp;
it could become the perfect prescription.

